Derived components and their provenance
---------------------------------------
The following components are derived from external research codebases. Their
licensing is being confirmed with the respective authors before any
distribution beyond the immediate research group (see "Status", below).

1. PanguWeather-derived deterministic models
   - Files: physicsnemo/experimental/models/pangu_plasim/**,
     physicsnemo/experimental/models/sfno_plasim/**,
     examples/weather/ai_rossby/loss.py (loss formulation).
   - Derived from: the PanguWeather v2.0 training stack (the
     "PanguWeather-e3sm" / "PanguWeather-plasim" forks), which is itself
     derived from NVIDIA's makani / FourCastNet stack (Apache-2.0) and from the
     original Pangu-Weather architecture (Bi et al.,
     https://github.com/198808xc/Pangu-Weather).
   - Copyright / license: Copyright (c) 2026 Alexander Wikner / The University
     of Chicago; released under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (consistent with
     the makani / FourCastNet ancestry). Confirmed 2026-07-09.

2. amip-derived diffusion models and recipe
   - Files: physicsnemo/experimental/models/amip_si/**,
     physicsnemo/experimental/diffusion/**,
     examples/weather/ai_rossby/{train_diffusion,validate_diffusion,eval_diffusion}.py,
     tools/checkpoint_translation/amip_si.py.
   - Derived from: the "amip" diffusion codebase, @ commit 497827e (the
     per-file "Vendored from the amip repo @ commit 497827e" markers).
   - Copyright / license: Copyright (c) 2026 Anthony Zhou, Carnegie Mellon
     University (ayz2@andrew.cmu.edu). Used with the author's permission
     (confirmed 2026-07-09) and released here under the Apache License,
     Version 2.0. The vendored amip files
     (physicsnemo/experimental/models/amip_si/**,
     physicsnemo/experimental/diffusion/**) carry his copyright line.

3. EDM diffusion core
   - File: physicsnemo/experimental/diffusion/__init__.py (EDMSchedulerModule)
     and related.
   - Modeled on EDM (Karras et al.). This code tracks the Apache-2.0 EDM
     implementation already shipped in PhysicsNeMo — NOT the non-commercial
     (CC-BY-NC-SA) NVIDIA EDM reference implementation. TODO — confirm.

Status (2026-07-09)
-------------------
Release scope: internal research group only. Author sign-off for both derived
components (PanguWeather-derived — A. Wikner; amip-derived — A. Zhou, CMU) has
been obtained, and copyright is recorded above. The EDM item (3) remains a
technical confirmation, not a legal blocker. A public release would still
